\ Compare exact wide counters against the six existing short day vectors.
\ This exercises the native-to-wide adapter and every wide counter
\ using values already established independently by the original
\ short source-level examples.

To compare a native calendar question with wide counters:
  Answer the example.
  Convert the example's calculation day into a wide signed day.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1,
    put "Conversion of the native calculation day failed." into the check report; exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide calendar example's calculation day.
  Convert the example's requested day into a wide signed day.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1,
    put "Conversion of the native requested day failed." into the check report; exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide calendar example's requested day.
  Answer the wide calendar example.
  Convert the example's calculation count to a string.
  If the wide calendar example's calculation count is not the string,
    put "Wide and native calculation counts disagree." into the check report; exit.
  Convert the example's requested count to a string.
  If the wide calendar example's requested count is not the string,
    put "Wide and native requested counts disagree." into the check report; exit.
  Convert the example's day distance to a string.
  If the wide calendar example's day distance is not the string,
    put "Wide and native inclusive day distances disagree." into the check report; exit.
  Convert the example's day sum to a string.
  If the wide calendar example's day sum is not the string,
    put "Wide and native counter sums disagree." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day direction is not the example's day direction,
    put "Wide and native directions disagree." into the check report; exit.

